  "query_preview": "the Small craft Advisory through 3 PM Friday. Seas of 6 to 8\nfeet and gentle to fresh winds will continue through this time, \nbefore gradually subsiding.\n\nPohnpei: \nThe heavier rainfall has moved off to your north and west, but\nscattered showers remain possible through Friday. Similar to Kosrae,\nfrequent gusts to 30 knots remain likely. As such, your Small Craft \nAdvisory also remains in effect through 3 PM Friday. Seas of 7 to 9 \nfeet and gentle to fresh winds will continue through this time, \nbefore gradually subsiding.\n\nMajuro: \nAlthough you have no headlines in place, the monsoon trough located \njust north of you continues to produce scattered showers. This looks \nto continue through Friday night, before shower coverage decreases to\nisolated for the weekend. Winds will be light to gentle with seas of\n4 to 6 feet.\n\nWestern Micronesia...\nChuuk:\nThe main changes to the forecast were to hoist a Small Craft Advisory\nat Chuuk, beginning 5 PM Friday and continuing through 5 PM Sunday.\nAs Tropical Depression Champi (29W) continues to strengthen into a\ntropical storm over the next 12 to 24 hours, an expanding wind field\nwill commence. Sustained gentle to moderate winds will become \nmoderate to fresh on Saturday. For now, we have frequent gusts to 30 \nkt as a start, but depending how the monsoon inflow band sets up, and\nhow Champi evolves, this may need to be revisited. An increasing \nnortheast to north swell meeting the southwest swell will add a layer\nof chop to the seas by early next week. Intra-island travel is \nhighly discouraged from late Friday afternoon into early next week to\naccount for this. As for precipitation, scattered showers will \ncontinue through at least the first part of the weekend, becoming \nisolated by early next week.\n\nPalau:\nLight to gentle winds will become gentle to moderate by Tuesday, with\nseas and surf building for the latter half of the week. Scattered\noragraphically-induced showers may need to be added to the forecast\nFriday into Saturday, but for now we didn't include this as we want\nto see how the pattern reorientates as TD Champi (29W) evolved as it\napproaches the Marianas. Otherwise, isolated showers remain possible.\n\nYap:\nThe main story here is a northeast swell looks to arrive for the\nearly to middle portion of next week, as Tropical Depression Champi \n(29W) continues to strengthen as it passes through and west of the \nMarianas. Otherwise, isolated showers remain possible.",
